{
  "subtype": "what_if",
  "outcome_variable": "resolution_time",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "ticket_type_primary",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": true,
      "rationale": "The query explicitly targets 'ticket types that create the heaviest agent workload' as the lever to reduce. This is the intervention variable and is directly named."
    },
    {
      "name": "agent_assignment",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Which agent handles a ticket can influence both the ticket type routed to them (specialization) and the resolution time (agent skill/speed), making it a common cause. Not named in the query."
    },
    {
      "name": "ticket_scope_extent",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Scope (single user vs enterprise-wide) plausibly affects both the ticket type distribution and resolution time, acting as a common cause. Not named in the query."
    },
    {
      "name": "ticket_complexity_judgment",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Intrinsic complexity drives both which ticket type/workload a ticket represents and how long it takes to resolve. A common cause not named in the query. (Arguably borderline with mediator, but as a pre-treatment intrinsic property it functions as a confounder.)"
    }
  ],
  "treatment_present": true,
  "treatment_columns": ["ticket_type_primary"],
  "treatment_intervenable": true,
  "confounders": [
    {"name": "agent_assignment", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.7},
    {"name": "ticket_scope_extent", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.75},
    {"name": "ticket_complexity_judgment", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.6}
  ],
  "confounder_quality": 0.7,
  "rationale": "The added set correctly instantiates a what-if intervention. ticket_type_primary is a genuine intervenable treatment: it is the settable lever named in the query (ticket types whose workload could be 'reduced'), and it is manipulable via routing/policy rather than being an immutable attribute. Three additional columns serve as plausible confounders -- common causes of both ticket type/workload and resolution time -- none of which are named in the query, which is exactly the capability under test. Agent assignment and ticket scope are solid confounders; complexity is somewhat borderline (could be read as a mediator of workload) but is best treated as a pre-treatment intrinsic driver. Overall this satisfies both parts of the technical claim: an intervenable treatment plus non-trivial, query-external confounders adjusted for before reading off the counterfactual effect."
}
